<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <!--
      Two kinds of key live here, and they do different things.

      allow-jit is the one runtime exception Electron needs: V8 writes machine
      code at run time, and this lets it do so through MAP_JIT and nothing
      wider. The other exceptions in electron-builder's template (unsigned
      executable memory, DYLD variables, library validation) are left out; each
      loosens only this binary, and the CLI Zetrem runs is a separate
      executable under its own signature, so none of them would reach it.

      The rest are resource-access entitlements, and they grant nothing by
      themselves. macOS charges what a child process does to the app that
      spawned it (the "responsible process"), so when an agent Zetrem started
      sends an Apple event, opens the camera or reads Contacts, it is Zetrem
      that macOS asks the person about. Under the hardened runtime that
      question is only asked when the matching entitlement is here; without
      it the request is refused with no dialog. The person still decides, and
      System Settings still records the answer under Zetrem.

      Bluetooth and USB are documented by Apple for sandboxed apps; they are
      listed so nothing an agent might reach for is left to fail silently.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>

    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.bluetooth</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.usb</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.location</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.addressbook</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.photos-library</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
